#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training.rst:5
msgid "DisplayPort Link Training"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:49
msgid ""
"This documents the Intel DisplayPort link training implementation and its "
"internal interfaces, with a current focus on link recovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:52
msgid "Documentation of the full link training procedure is not yet included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:54
msgid ""
"The Intel DP link recovery logic governs how the driver reacts to link "
"training failures and to links that degrade asynchronously after a "
"previously successful training. Recovery is first attempted via automatic "
"retraining (``autoretrain``) and, when that is no longer possible, by "
"selecting fallback link configurations and notifying userspace to recover "
"the link via a modeset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:64
msgid ""
"After the first link training failure following initialization or a "
"previously successful training, recovery is first attempted by the driver "
"via automatic retraining, without userspace involvement. During this phase, "
"a given link configuration is attempted twice before being abandoned: after "
"the initial link training failure, an automatic retraining modeset is "
"performed with the same link parameters, constituting the second attempt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:72
msgid ""
"Once automatic retraining is no longer possible, recovery is delegated to "
"userspace, which must select a new modeset configuration, as the kernel must "
"not do so. From this point onwards, each link configuration may be attempted "
"only once as userspace iterates through alternative configurations. A "
"successful link training restores the automatic retraining model for "
"subsequent failures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:79
msgid ""
"The failure of the last automatic retraining attempt is reported to "
"userspace, and from that point onward the driver notifies userspace of each "
"subsequent failure. This allows userspace to both initiate recovery via "
"modesets and observe the outcome of those recovery attempts, even when no "
"further fallback configurations remain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:85
msgid ""
"Link training failures are always reported to userspace, even when they "
"result from a kernel-internal modeset. Such modesets only re-apply the "
"existing userspace-provided state and must not modify it. A failure "
"triggered by such a modeset is therefore treated the same as a link "
"degradation after a previously successful training, and recovery is handled "
"by userspace in place of the kernel caller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/intel-display/dp-link-training:7:
#: ../drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_link_training.c:95
msgid ""
"The following execution contexts (A/B/C) describe how the different recovery "
"states are reached but are not themselves implementation states. The actual "
"state machine is defined by :c:type:`enum "
"intel_dp_link_training_recovery_state "
"<intel_dp_link_training_recovery_state>`."
msgstr ""

